        "original_id": "21989983-1650-5c51-af02-d733e76b2c96",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Hetfield, Rick Rubin, Bob Rock\n- Organizations: Metallica\n- Products: \"Enter Sandman\", \"Metallica\", Death Magnetic\n- Concepts: children's nightmares\n\nFacts:\n- In 1991, Metallica released the album \"Metallica\".\n- In 1991, the album \"Metallica\" was not produced by Bob Rock.\n- The album \"Metallica\" produced five well-known singles: \"Enter Sandman\", \"The Unforgiven\", \"Nothing Else Matters\", \"Wherever I May Roam\", and \"Sad but True\".\n- \"Enter Sandman\" is a song by the American heavy metal band Metallica.\n- James Hetfield wrote the lyrics to \"Enter Sandman\".\n- The lyrics of \"Enter Sandman\" deal with the concept of a child's nightmares.\n- Death Magnetic was Metallica's first album produced by Rick Rubin.\n- Death Magnetic was Metallica's first album since \"Metallica\" (1991) that was not produced by Bob Rock.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
